# QUAKE 1 MATERIALS
#
# Written by tools/q1matdev.py from the rerelease's paks (id1/<episode>/pak0.pak)
# and Matt's RTX Remix project. Re-run it after changing either; everything
# after the END marker below is kept.
#
# NAMES. A Quake 1 map's texture "metal1_1" is textures/q1/metal1_1, "*water0"
# is textures/q1/#water0 (bsp_q1.c). A rerelease md5 skin is its .lmp's name:
# progs/ogre_00_00. An .mdl skin is progs/<model>_mdl_<skin>_<frame>
# (progs/ogre_mdl_00_00), a sprite frame progs/<sprite>_spr_<frame>.
#
# texture_base names a copy of the texture in materialDev/, as the engine makes
# it from the palette (fullbright colours included), so editing that PNG
# changes the game. It is left commented where several images share the name
# - different maps or episodes with their own "metal1_1" - since one file
# would replace them all, and on fences ({ textures), whose see-through
# pixels the engine's own copy handles. The commented _n / _rough / _metal /
# _height / _emissive lines are where PBR maps go: make the file, uncomment the
# line, then "mat reload".
#
# GLOW. Quake's fullbright colours (palette 224-254) glow by themselves: the
# engine makes a wall's <name>_light from them, and a skin names its
# materialDev copy. A wall texture where more than 0.5% of the pixels are
# fullbright is also a LIGHT (is_light 1) - with no light entities drawn, that
# and the sky are what light a map Matt has not lit himself. Fewer than that
# glow but cast nothing, and so does every skin (a monster's eyes would make it
# a light).
#
# MATT'S REMIX MATERIALS (347 entries) come first, then the stubs (2311,
# of which 217 are lights). From Remix:
#   - his normal maps are DirectX (+Y down), this renderer's convention, so
#     they are used as painted. Remix showed them with green flipped (it
#     ingested them as OpenGL), so a bump may now read the other way round.
#   - emissive_factor = Remix emissive_intensity x 0.025 (Remix's default 40 is 1
#     here). The same K sets his lights' brightness (maps/lights/q1/*.cfg).
#   - a Remix constant metallic is a solid "*M1" metallic map times
#     metalness_factor; a constant roughness clears the roughness map and gives
#     roughness_override. Where he set no roughness at all, 0.5 - Remix's
#     default for an edited material - so it looks as it did there.
#   - what has no equivalent is noted on the entry: sprite sheets (a still
#     frame is used where one exists), particle emitters, water transmittance.

# === BEGIN q1matdev.py generated block - rewritten by every run ===

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FROM MATT'S RTX REMIX PROJECT (F:/VKQuakeSrc/qss-run/QuakeRTX), 347 entries
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

